  "fullDescription": "Bold painterly roses in crimson and pink burst across a cream background in this lush chintz-style repeat pattern.\n\nThis surface pattern features large-scale garden roses rendered in a thick, impasto oil-painting style with visible brushwork that gives each bloom a tactile, dimensional quality. Deep crimson roses anchor the composition while soft pink roses with golden stamens add tonal variation. Sky blue hydrangea-like clusters and tiny forget-me-not sprays weave between the blooms, creating rhythmic secondary movement. Small white daisy-like flowers with yellow centres, red berry clusters, and plump rosebuds fill the negative space, ensuring no area feels sparse. Rich emerald and hunter green foliage with painterly highlights ties the palette together against an off-white warm cream ground.\n\nThe overall aesthetic sits at the intersection of English chintz, vintage botanical illustration, and folk art oil painting — evoking the maximalist floral tradition seen in Victorian fabric design, Grandmillenial décor trends, and cottage-core aesthetics. The mood is romantic, abundant, and joyful with a handcrafted warmth. This pattern is ideally suited for fabric yardage, quilting cotton, dress and blouse material, tote bags, gift wrap, wallpaper, scrapbook paper, journal covers, throw pillow sublimation, POD mugs and phone cases, Canva design projects, and Procreate or Photoshop digital backgrounds.",
